From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSBedded <noreply@jsbedded.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Make the embed source list link without the OS modules

Not sent upstream yet (part of upstream ask 4 in JSBedded's
firmware/engines/ant/README.md: a minimal embed source list).

At this version the reactor's source list (packages/wasm/meson.build)
no longer links: src/ant.c calls the event loop, the HTTP pool, watch
mode, workers, N-API, Wasm, ES module helpers and the cleanup and GC
hooks of about twenty modules unconditionally, and includes loop.h,
watch.h, modules/http.h and modules/websocket.h, which need <uv.h>.
The promise code, the arena allocator and the stringify helpers it
needs are not in the list at all. The embed microtask queue also
predates the await_resume_job handshake that sugar.c and promise.c use.

- The embed list (sources.json "embed", and the reactor's
  core_sources) adds the OS-free files the core needs:
  src/gc/arena.c, src/modules/promise.c, src/stringify.c,
  src/modules/domexception.c and src/index.c.
- src/embed/microtasks.c replaces the queue in src/embed/stubs.c with
  the job part of src/modules/timer.c (same job kinds and processing,
  without timers, immediates, next ticks or libuv), plus the embed
  interrupt check between jobs.
- src/embed/module_stubs.c provides the hooks of the modules that are
  not built: no-ops for lifecycle and GC hooks, "not available" for
  import.meta.resolve, false for the ESM URL checks, a file:// URL for
  import.meta.url, no printf-style substitution in console.log, no
  typed arrays, the embed built-ins for node:vm realms, and "not
  available" for import().
- src/embed/jit_stub.c also covers sv_jit_drop_func_code and
  sv_jit_await_resume (nothing is ever JIT-compiled).
- src/embed/stubs.c: gc_clear_napi_weak_refs takes the
  gc_weak_key_alive_fn its header declares.
- Under ANT_EMBED, src/ant.c skips the four libuv headers and declares
  the seven functions it uses from them; modules/atomics.h leaves out
  the pthread-based Atomics.wait queues, which only atomics.c uses.
